slug: pulmonary-rehabilitation-copd
title: Pulmonary Rehabilitation for COPD — Exercise Is the Treatment
area: Cardiorespiratory
level: Foundation
best: 3rd year onwards
minutes: 13
hook: People with COPD stop moving because they get breathless, then get more breathless because they stop moving. Pulmonary rehabilitation breaks this spiral, and it improves breathlessness and quality of life more than most medicines. Learn how to assess, train and keep these patients safe. || COPD ke mareez saans phoolne ki wajah se harkat chhor dete hain, phir harkat chhorne se aur zyada saans phoolti hai. Pulmonary rehabilitation is chakkar ko torti hai, aur saans aur zindagi ke maiyar ko aksar dawaiyon se zyada behtar karti hai. Seekhein in mareezon ka assessment, training aur hifazat kaise karein.
goal: By the end, you'll explain the breathlessness spiral, assess with the MRC dyspnoea scale and a walk test, prescribe endurance and strength training for a 6 to 8 week programme, use oxygen saturation safely and teach recovery positions. || End tak aap saans phoolne ka chakkar samjhayenge, MRC dyspnoea scale aur walk test se assessment karenge, 6 se 8 hafte ke programme ke liye endurance aur strength training likhenge, oxygen saturation ko mehfooz tareeqe se istemal karenge aur recovery positions sikhayenge.

say: **Pulmonary rehabilitation** is a supervised programme of **exercise training and education**, usually **twice a week for 6 to 8 weeks**, for people with chronic lung disease who are limited by breathlessness (typically **MRC grade 3 or above**). It does not change lung function tests much, but it trains the **leg and arm muscles** to use oxygen better, reduces the fear of breathlessness, and teaches self-management. People have less breathlessness, walk further, feel better and are **readmitted to hospital less often** after a flare-up. || **Pulmonary rehabilitation** **exercise training aur taleem** ka nigrani wala programme hai, aam taur par **hafte mein do baar 6 se 8 hafte**, purani phephron ki bimari walon ke liye jinhein saans phoolna rokta hai (aam taur par **MRC grade 3 ya zyada**). Yeh lung function tests ko zyada nahi badalta, magar **taangon aur bazuon ke muscles** ko oxygen behtar istemal karna sikhata hai, saans phoolne ka khauf kam karta hai, aur apna khayal rakhna sikhata hai. Logon ki saans kam phoolti hai, woh zyada chal paate hain, behtar mehsoos karte hain aur flare ke baad **hospital mein dobara kam dakhil** hote hain.
analogy: COPD lungs are like a **small, old engine** you cannot replace. Pulmonary rehab does not rebuild the engine; it makes the **car lighter and more efficient** — stronger muscles need less oxygen for the same work, and a calmer driver wastes less fuel. || COPD wale phephre ek **chhote, purane engine** jaise hain jo badla nahi ja sakta. Pulmonary rehab engine dobara nahi banata; yeh **gaari ko halka aur behtar** banata hai — mazboot muscles ko ek hi kaam ke liye kam oxygen chahiye, aur pursukoon driver kam fuel zaya karta hai.
steps: Running a pulmonary rehab session || Pulmonary rehab session chalana
step: Assess at the start :: Record the MRC dyspnoea grade, a walk test (6-minute walk or incremental shuttle walk), oxygen saturation at rest and on exercise, and a quality-of-life score (for example CAT). Check that medicines and inhalers are being used correctly. || Shuru mein assessment :: MRC dyspnoea grade, walk test (6-minute walk ya incremental shuttle walk), aaram aur exercise par oxygen saturation, aur zindagi ke maiyar ka score (maslan CAT) likhein. Check karein ke dawaiyan aur inhalers theek istemal ho rahe hain.
step: Endurance training :: Walking or cycling for about 20 to 30 minutes in total (intervals are fine), at a breathlessness of about 3 to 4 on the 0 to 10 Borg scale, or about 60 to 80 percent of the walk-test speed. || Endurance training :: Kul takreeban 20 se 30 minute chalna ya cycling (intervals theek hain), 0 se 10 Borg scale par takreeban 3 se 4 saans phoolne ke saath, ya walk-test ki raftaar ka takreeban 60 se 80 percent.
step: Strength training :: Legs and arms: sit-to-stand, step-ups, wall push-ups, arm raises with light weights; 2 to 3 sets of 8 to 12 repetitions, progressed when easy. Breathe out on the effort. || Strength training :: Taangen aur bazu: sit-to-stand, step-ups, wall push-ups, halke wazan ke saath bazu uthana; 8 se 12 repetitions ke 2 se 3 sets, aasan hone par barhayein. Zor lagate hue saans bahar.
step: Teach recovery and self-management :: Forward-lean positions, pursed-lip breathing and pacing to recover from breathlessness; inhaler technique; spotting a flare-up early; staying active after the programme ends. || Recovery aur apna khayal sikhayein :: Saans phoolne se sambhalne ke liye aage jhukne ki positions, pursed-lip breathing aur pacing; inhaler ka tareeqa; flare jaldi pehchanna; programme ke baad bhi fa'aal rehna.

check: What does pulmonary rehabilitation mainly improve? || Pulmonary rehabilitation zyada tar kya behtar karti hai?
ok: Breathlessness, exercise capacity and quality of life, through trained muscles and better self-management || Saans phoolna, exercise ki salahiyat aur zindagi ka maiyar, trained muscles aur behtar khud-nigrani ke zariye || Yes — the lungs change little; the person changes a lot. || Haan — phephre kam badalte hain; insaan bohat badalta hai.
no: It cures the damage in the lungs || Yeh phephron ka nuqsan theek kar deti hai || COPD damage is permanent. || COPD ka nuqsan mustaqil hai.
no: It mainly raises FEV1 to normal || Yeh zyada tar FEV1 ko normal kar deti hai || Lung function changes very little. || Lung function bohat kam badalta hai.
compare: Endurance or strength training? || Endurance ya strength training?
head: Feature || Khasiyat ;; Endurance || Endurance ;; Strength || Strength
row: Examples || Misalen ;; Walking, cycling, stairs || Chalna, cycling, seedhiyan ;; Sit-to-stand, step-ups, weights || Sit-to-stand, step-ups, wazan
row: Dose || Dosage ;; 20 to 30 minutes, Borg 3 to 4 || 20 se 30 minute, Borg 3 se 4 ;; 2 to 3 sets of 8 to 12 || 8 se 12 ke 2 se 3 sets
row: Main benefit || Mukhya faida ;; Walk further with less breathlessness || Kam saans phoolne ke saath zyada chalna ;; Stronger legs for daily tasks || Rozmarra kaamon ke liye mazboot taangen
row: Tip || Mashwara ;; Intervals if continuous is too hard || Musalsal mushkil ho to intervals ;; Breathe out on effort || Zor par saans bahar
memory: **Breathless is not dangerous; desaturation is.** Being out of breath during exercise is expected and safe. A falling oxygen saturation is what needs action. || **Saans phoolna khatarnak nahi; saturation girna hai.** Exercise mein saans phoolna mutawaqqa aur mehfooz hai. Oxygen saturation ka girna woh cheez hai jis par qadam uthana zaroori hai.
mistake: **Stopping exercise every time the patient is breathless.** Short-lived, recoverable breathlessness is the training stimulus. Teach a recovery position and pursed-lip breathing, let it settle, and carry on. Stop for chest pain, dizziness, or saturation that falls and does not recover. || **Har baar saans phoolne par exercise rok dena.** Thori der ka, theek ho jane wala saans phoolna hi training ka stimulus hai. Recovery position aur pursed-lip breathing sikhayein, sambhalne dein, aur jaari rakhein. Seene ke dard, chakkar, ya girti aur wapas na aane wali saturation par rok dein.
check: During a walk, saturation drops from 94 to 86 percent and stays low after a rest. What should you do? || Chalte hue saturation 94 se 86 percent par gir jati hai aur aaram ke baad bhi kam rehti hai. Kya karna chahiye?
ok: Stop, rest, follow the oxygen plan and discuss oxygen during exercise with the medical team || Rok dein, aaram karayein, oxygen plan par amal karein aur exercise mein oxygen ke baare mein medical team se baat karein || Yes — sustained desaturation needs assessment, often oxygen on exertion. || Haan — musalsal kam saturation ko assessment chahiye, aksar mehnat par oxygen.
no: Push on — breathlessness is good training || Jaari rakhein — saans phoolna achhi training hai || Breathlessness is fine; sustained low oxygen is not. || Saans phoolna theek hai; musalsal kam oxygen nahi.
no: Ignore it; pulse oximeters are often wrong || Nazarandaz karein; pulse oximeter aksar ghalat hote hain || Check the reading (good signal, warm fingers), but act on a true fall. || Reading check karein (achha signal, garam ungliyan), magar asal girawat par qadam uthayein.
check: When is the best time to start pulmonary rehabilitation after a hospital stay for a COPD flare-up? || COPD flare ke baad hospital se aane par pulmonary rehabilitation kab shuru karna behtar hai?
ok: Within about 4 weeks of discharge || Discharge ke takreeban 4 hafte ke andar || Yes — early rehab after a flare reduces readmissions. || Haan — flare ke baad jaldi rehab dobara dakhil hone ko kam karta hai.
no: Only after a year of stability || Sirf ek saal ki behtari ke baad || Waiting loses the window of benefit. || Intezar faide ka waqt zaya kar deta hai.
no: Never — it is unsafe after a flare-up || Kabhi nahi — flare ke baad yeh ghair-mehfooz hai || Supervised rehab after a flare is safe and recommended. || Flare ke baad nigrani wala rehab mehfooz aur tajweez kiya gaya hai.
clinic: **Make it fit local life.** Many patients have smoked or cooked over wood or dung fires for years. Use stairs, walking routes in the neighbourhood and water bottles as weights, and run the programme where transport is easy. A family member who learns the exercises helps the patient keep going after the 8 weeks. || **Isay maqami zindagi ke mutabiq banayein.** Bohat se mareez saalon se cigarette peete rahe ya lakri ya uplon ki aag par khana pakate rahe. Seedhiyan, mohalle ke chalne ke raaste aur pani ki botalen wazan ke taur par istemal karein, aur programme wahan chalayein jahan aana jana aasan ho. Exercises seekhne wala ghar ka fard mareez ko 8 hafte ke baad bhi jaari rakhne mein madad deta hai.
reveal: Why does training the legs help a lung disease? || Taangon ki training phephron ki bimari mein kyun madad karti hai? || In COPD the leg muscles become weak and inefficient from inactivity and inflammation, so they produce lactate early and drive faster breathing. Trained muscles do the same work with less oxygen and less carbon dioxide, so breathing demand falls and the person can walk further before becoming breathless. || COPD mein ghair-fa'aaliyat aur sozish se taangon ke muscles kamzor aur kam-kaar ho jate hain, is liye woh jaldi lactate banate hain aur saans tez karwate hain. Trained muscles wohi kaam kam oxygen aur kam carbon dioxide ke saath karte hain, is liye saans ki zaroorat kam hoti hai aur shakhs saans phoolne se pehle zyada chal sakta hai.
case: A 64-year-old former smoker with COPD (MRC grade 4) stops after 100 metres to catch his breath. His 6-minute walk is 240 metres, his resting saturation is 93 percent and falls to 89 percent on walking, recovering within a minute of rest. || He is a typical candidate for pulmonary rehabilitation; brief, recovering desaturation can be managed with interval training and monitoring. || An 8-week programme, twice weekly: interval walking at Borg 3 to 4, sit-to-stand and arm exercises, pursed-lip breathing and forward-lean recovery, inhaler check and a home walking plan. || His walk increases to 310 metres, he climbs stairs at home with one rest instead of three, and he keeps walking daily with his son.
safety: **Stop and seek medical help** for chest pain, new or rapidly worsening breathlessness at rest, confusion or drowsiness, blue lips, coughing blood, or saturation that stays well below the patient's target despite rest. **Delay rehab** during an acute flare-up, uncontrolled heart failure or unstable angina. Patients on oxygen must follow their prescribed flow; a target of 88 to 92 percent is common for people at risk of carbon dioxide retention. || **Rok kar medical madad lein** seene mein dard, aaram mein nayi ya tezi se barhti saans ki takleef, uljhan ya ghunoodgi, neele honth, khoon wali khansi, ya aaram ke bawajood mareez ke target se kaafi kam rehne wali saturation par. **Rehab mulatvi karein** shadeed flare, be-qaboo heart failure ya unstable angina ke dauran. Oxygen wale mareez apna likha hua flow follow karein; carbon dioxide rokne ke khatre walon ke liye 88 se 92 percent aam target hai.
summary: Pulmonary rehabilitation is 6 to 8 weeks of supervised exercise and education for people limited by breathlessness (MRC 3 and above). || Pulmonary rehabilitation saans phoolne se mehdood logon (MRC 3 aur zyada) ke liye 6 se 8 hafte ki nigrani wali exercise aur taleem hai.
summary: Train endurance (20 to 30 minutes at Borg 3 to 4, intervals allowed) and strength (2 to 3 sets of 8 to 12), and teach recovery positions and pursed-lip breathing. || Endurance (Borg 3 se 4 par 20 se 30 minute, intervals ki ijazat) aur strength (8 se 12 ke 2 se 3 sets) ki training dein, aur recovery positions aur pursed-lip breathing sikhayein.
summary: Breathlessness is expected; sustained desaturation, chest pain and confusion are not — and rehab started soon after a flare-up reduces readmissions. || Saans phoolna mutawaqqa hai; musalsal saturation girna, seene ka dard aur uljhan nahi — aur flare ke baad jaldi shuru kiya rehab dobara dakhil hone ko kam karta hai.
card: Who is referred to pulmonary rehab? || Pulmonary rehab ke liye kis ko bheja jata hai? || People with chronic lung disease limited by breathlessness, usually MRC grade 3 or above. || Purani phephron ki bimari wale jinhein saans phoolna rokta hai, aam taur par MRC grade 3 ya zyada.
card: Typical length of a programme? || Programme ki aam muddat? || 6 to 8 weeks, about twice a week, supervised. || 6 se 8 hafte, takreeban hafte mein do baar, nigrani mein.
card: Target breathlessness during endurance training? || Endurance training mein saans phoolne ka target? || About 3 to 4 on the 0 to 10 Borg scale. || 0 se 10 Borg scale par takreeban 3 se 4.
card: Best time to start after a flare-up? || Flare ke baad shuru karne ka behtareen waqt? || Within about 4 weeks of hospital discharge. || Hospital se discharge ke takreeban 4 hafte ke andar.
deeper: Breathlessness — positions, pacing and breathing control || /learn/breathlessness-self-management || The recovery skills taught in every session. || Har session mein sikhayi jane wali recovery ki maharat.
deeper: The six-minute walk test || /learn/six-minute-walk-test-breathlessness || The main test for measuring progress. || Behtari naapne ka mukhya test.
source: Spruit MA, Singh SJ, Garvey C, et al. An official American Thoracic Society/European Respiratory Society statement: key concepts and advances in pulmonary rehabilitation. Am J Respir Crit Care Med 2013;188(8):e13-e64. || ATS ERS statement key concepts advances pulmonary rehabilitation 2013
source: McCarthy B, Casey D, Devane D, Murphy K, Murphy E, Lacasse Y. Pulmonary rehabilitation for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Cochrane Database Syst Rev 2015;(2):CD003793. || pulmonary rehabilitation chronic obstructive pulmonary disease Cochrane 2015
source: Puhan MA, Gimeno-Santos E, Cates CJ, Troosters T. Pulmonary rehabilitation following exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Cochrane Database Syst Rev 2016;12:CD005305. || pulmonary rehabilitation following exacerbations COPD Cochrane
